This PR includes the simple incremental learning method for the classification,
It simply limits the total epochs by checking the task and the model name since each model has a different iteration time.
To reduce the validation time, added the random sampling logic.

Potential risk (will be resolved further)
* If there are too many images at the train, due to the effect of mem cache, iter_time will be largely different. However, simple incremental learning focuses to the interactive training, this PR not consider this case.
* During the sampling the validation dataset, some classes could be vanished. In the simple incremental learning, we don't care about the accuracy and it is hard to predict the E2E time (train+val) if there are many validation data. That's the reason why I added the random sample logic for the validation set. It could be updated at further PR. 

There is no test case implementation, yet. It'll be implemented.
Just want to share the way of the implementation and listening the feedback 

